{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nr=json.load(open('/workspace/runtime_context.json'))\nprint(list(r))\nfor k,v in r.items():\n if k not in ('context','study_schema','candidate_api'): print(k, json.dumps(v,indent=2))\nprint('CONTEXT KEYS',list(r['context']))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"/bin/bash: warning: setlocale: LC_ALL: cannot change locale (C.UTF-8)\n/bin/bash: warning: setlocale: LC_ALL: cannot change locale (C.UTF-8)\n['phase', 'expected_files', 'context', 'study_schema', 'required_study_protocol_ref', 'reference_format', 'action', 'candidate_api']\nphase \"propose\"\nexpected_files [\n  \"proposal.json\"\n]\nrequired_study_protocol_ref \"1a10f150c0b3977043072cd01f67a339c5c476f15c7847d04fa3acf9ce71e216\"\nreference_format \"Use allowed_observation_ids verbatim for local evidence. Descriptive references are accepted when they contain a complete known ID. Correct any previous_runtime_error before submitting; its failed costs remain charged.\"\naction \"Read candidate.py and baseline_reference.py, diagnose an observed limitation, check primary nearest work, and implement a feasible candidate. Write proposal.json containing study (matching study_schema), parent_trial (existing trial ID), and variants (1-4 objects with distinct name, file basename ending .py, role candidate/control, config object, and note). At least one candidate is required. Add key ablations or matched controls for the claimed mechanism when feasible; reference existing matched trials as controls where justified. Each variant is a standalone module. Do not run training. New architecture choices come from evidence; industry cards do not mandate them.\"\nCONTEXT KEYS ['history', 'allowed_observation_ids', 'previous_runtime_error', 'trajectory_index', 'incumbent', 'remaining_seconds', 'protocol', 'method', 'budget_scope', 'no_test_feedback', 'knowledge_revision', 'knowledge_review', 'latest_knowledge_usage']\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
