{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_30","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'python3 /workspace/tools.py read unirank-benchmark-v2 --find INFNet --lines 50'","aggregated_output":"/bin/bash: warning: setlocale: LC_ALL: cannot change locale (C.UTF-8)\n/bin/bash: warning: setlocale: LC_ALL: cannot change locale (C.UTF-8)\n{\n  \"id\": \"unirank-benchmark-v2\",\n  \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/html/2607.19987v2\",\n  \"version\": \"arxiv:2607.19987v2\",\n  \"access_scope\": \"Cached section2.3 method descriptions; not an original-method full-paper audit.\",\n  \"text_sha256\": \"34ff9c412b35f3118aae377faca5f658d7bffac0b4ef1c12a4eb0c7937372789\",\n  \"total_lines\": 39,\n  \"start_line\": 29,\n  \"next_line\": 40,\n  \"truncated\": false,\n  \"text\": \"29: MixFormer (Huang et al., 2026a) mixes non-sequential queries, uses cross-attention to retrieve information from the updated sequence, and fuses the resulting representations.\\n30: •\\n31: INFNet (Li et al., 2025b) organizes categorical, sequential, and task tokens around a hub for layer-wise aggregation and broadcasting.\\n32: •\\n33: EST (Liu et al., 2026) uses cross-attention to sequence representations and feature-specific feed-forward layers.\\n34: •\\n35: TokenFormer (Zhou et al., 2026) represents fields, histories, and targets as tokens with full interaction and sliding-window Flex Attention.\\n36: •\\n37: LONGER (Chai et al., 2025) encodes local groups with inner Transformers and joins compressed long-term history with recent queries.\\n38: •\\n39: UltraHSTU (Ding et al., 2026) extends HSTU-style sequential transduction (Zhai et al., 2024) with hybrid attention that combines sparse and full attention in each interaction layer.\"\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_31","type":"agent_message","text":"The earlier trials suggest gradient blocking contributes to the auxiliary losses, and a private embedding branch only partly recovered them at higher cost. I’ll test a narrower question: whether task-specific counts and content retain useful information that the merged feedback group loses.\n\nI’ll prepare three models with the same added head capacity and existing scorer: exact task summaries, task counts paired with merged content, and duplicated merged summaries. These comparisons separate retained content, task counts, and added capacity.\n"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_32","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('/workspace/candidate.py')\ns=p.read_text()\nstart=s.index('import torch')\ns='''\\\"\\\"\\\"Task-resolved moments without additional history scoring.\n\nInherit the incumbent's compressed scorer, source gates, age/behavior readout\nand towers. Add identical zero-output residual heads in all cells. Exact task\nsums preserve cart/fav/buy membership within each of ten temporal partitions;\ncentroid replacement keeps exact task counts but substitutes the union mean;\nunion replacement duplicates the existing union sums/counts for every task.\nAll cells execute the same task-mask sum operator and the existing 30-slot\nscorer. No event is scored again. Historical masks can overlap; these are not\nexclusive groups, current labels, or advertisement conversion attributions.\n\nTask summaries are weighted by the existing union-positive slot activation,\nthen exposed as totals, signed last-ten-minus-older sums and counts/100. The\nnew auxiliary paths detach item/action/scorer representations while retaining\ncontext gradients. Efficacy, efficiency and originality remain unverified.\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\\\n'''+s[start:]\ns=s.replace(\\\"    'residual_hidden_units': 32,\\\\n\\\", \\\"    'residual_hidden_units': 32,\\\\n    'identity_content': 'exact',\\\\n    'identity_hidden_units': 32,\\\\n\\\",1)\ns=s.replace(\\\"model_id='TemporalBehaviorReadout'\\\", \\\"model_id='TaskResolvedMoments'\\\")\ns=s.replace(\\\"behavior_readout='separate', residual_hidden_units=32, num_tasks=None,\\\", \\\"behavior_readout='separate', residual_hidden_units=32,\\\\n                 identity_content='exact', identity_hidden_units=32, num_tasks=None,\\\")\ns=s.replace(\\\"        self.behavior_readout = behavior_readout\\\\n\\\", \\\"\\\"\\\"        self.behavior_readout = behavior_readout\n        if temporal_readout \"'!= '\"'separate' or behavior_readout \"'!= '\"'separate':\n            raise ValueError('Freeze the incumbent marginal readouts')\n        if identity_content not in ('exact', 'centroid', 'union'):\n            raise ValueError('Unknown task-moment replacement')\n        if identity_hidden_units \"'!= 32:\n            raise ValueError('\"'Identity residual width is fixed at 32')\n        self.identity_content = identity_content\n\\\"\\\"\\\",1)\ns=s.replace(\\\"        self.model_to_device()\\\\n\\\", \\\"\\\"\\\"        # A separate RNG fork leaves every inherited parameter and the caller's\n        # CPU RNG unchanged. All replacement cells have identical new shapes,\n        # initialization and module order. Zero output reproduces the parent\n        # predictions initially; it does not promise trained-model equality.\n        with torch.random.fork_rng(devices=[]):\n            identity_width = (len(self.user_fields) * embedding_dim\n                              + self.key_width + 6 * self.value_width + 30)\n            self.identity_heads = nn.ModuleList([\n                nn.Sequential(nn.Linear(identity_width, identity_hidden_units),\n                              nn.ReLU(), nn.Linear(identity_hidden_units, 1))\n                for _ in feature_map.labels\n            ])\n            for head in self.identity_heads:\n                nn.init.zeros_(head[-1].weight)\n                nn.init.zeros_(head[-1].bias)\n        self.model_to_device()\n\\\"\\\"\\\",1)\ns=s.replace(\\\"        return context, target, values, mask, auxiliary\\\\n\\\", \\\"\\\"\\\"        # Preserve all three authorized task masks, including overlaps. The\n        # canonical order is independent of the FeatureMap label order.\n        task_members = torch.stack([\n            (task_masks[index] > 0) & mask.bool()\n            for index in self.auxiliary_indices\n        ], dim=1)\n        return context, target, values, mask, auxiliary, task_members\n\\\"\\\"\\\",1)\ninsert=s.index('    def forward(self, inputs):')\ns=s[:insert]+'''    def _identity_statistics(self, raw_values, mask, task_members, values, counts):\n        # [B,task,partition,event]; no extra scorer rows or parameters.\n        clean = torch.where(mask.bool().unsqueeze(-1), raw_values,\n                            torch.zeros_like(raw_values))\n        assignment = (task_members[:, :, None, :]\n                      & self.partition[None, None, :, :])\n        assignment = assignment.reshape(raw_values.shape[0], 30, 100).to(clean.dtype)\n        task_counts = assignment.sum(dim=-1).reshape(-1, 3, 10)\n        exact = torch.bmm(assignment, clean).reshape(-1, 3, 10, self.value_width)\n        union_means = values.reshape(-1, 10, 3, self.value_width)[:, :, 2, :]\n        union_counts = counts.reshape(-1, 10, 3)[:, :, 2]\n        centroid = task_counts.unsqueeze(-1) * union_means[:, None, :, :]\n        duplicated = (union_counts.unsqueeze(-1) * union_means)[:, None, :, :].expand(-1, 3, -1, -1)\n        # Compute all alternatives before replacement in every cell. Exact\n        # task counts stay visible in the exact/centroid pair. The union cell\n        # contains no resolved mask information on any path to a logit.\n        if self.identity_content == 'exact':\n            sums, exposed_counts = exact, task_counts\n        elif self.identity_content == 'centroid':\n            sums, exposed_counts = centroid, task_counts\n        else:\n            sums = duplicated\n            exposed_counts = union_counts[:, None, :].expand(-1, 3, -1)\n        return sums, exposed_counts\n\n    def _identity_readout(self, primary_weights, sums, counts):\n        # Each partition's existing union-positive score is reused for each\n        # task sum. Counts are already present in sums; never multiply twice.\n        weights = primary_weights.reshape(-1, 10, 3)[:, :, 2]\n        weighted = sums * weights[:, None, :, None]\n        total = weighted.sum(dim=2)\n        age = (weighted * self.age_sign.to(weighted.dtype)[None, None, :, None]).sum(dim=2)\n        # Counts are unweighted and FP32, on the fixed 100-event scale.\n        # Do not interpret them as rates per unit time: timestamps unavailable.\n        return torch.cat([total.flatten(1), age.flatten(1),\n                          counts.flatten(1) / 100.0], dim=-1)\n\n'''+s[insert:]\ns=s.replace(\\\"        context, target, values, mask, auxiliary = self._represent(inputs)\\\\n        values, counts = self._compress_both(values, mask, auxiliary)\\\\n\\\", \\\"\\\"\\\"        context, target, raw_values, mask, auxiliary, task_members = self._represent(inputs)\n        values, counts = self._compress_both(raw_values, mask, auxiliary)\n        identity_sums, identity_counts = self._identity_statistics(\n            raw_values, mask, task_members, values, counts)\n\\\"\\\"\\\",1)\ns=s.replace(\\\"        primary_strata, primary_readout = self._pool(primary_weights, values, counts)\\\\n\\\", \\\"\\\"\\\"        primary_strata, primary_readout = self._pool(primary_weights, values, counts)\n        identity = self._identity_readout(primary_weights, identity_sums, identity_counts)\n        # Scorer and both item/action sources are frozen to auxiliary losses.\n        # Computing this descriptor once also avoids another Dice population.\n        aux_identity = identity.detach() if self.training else identity\n\\\"\\\"\\\",1)\ns=s.replace(\\\"        for label, tower, head in zip(self.feature_map.labels, self.towers, self.residual_heads):\\\\n\\\", \\\"\\\"\\\"        for label, tower, head, identity_head in zip(\n                self.feature_map.labels, self.towers, self.residual_heads,\n                self.identity_heads):\n\\\"\\\"\\\",1)\ns=s.replace(\\\"                extra = (click_readout, primary_feedback, primary_behavior)\\\\n\\\", \\\"\\\"\\\"                extra = (click_readout, primary_feedback, primary_behavior)\n                identity_input = torch.cat([context, target, identity], dim=-1)\n\\\"\\\"\\\",1)\ns=s.replace(\\\"                extra = (feedback_readout, feedback, feedback_behavior)\\\\n\\\", \\\"\\\"\\\"                extra = (feedback_readout, feedback, feedback_behavior)\n                identity_input = torch.cat([aux_context, aux_target, aux_identity], dim=-1)\n\\\"\\\"\\\",1)\ns=s.replace(\\\"            logits = tower(features) + head(torch.cat((features,) + extra, dim=-1))\\\\n\\\", \\\"\\\"\\\"            logits = (tower(features) + head(torch.cat((features,) + extra, dim=-1))\n                      + identity_head(identity_input))\n\\\"\\\"\\\",1)\np.write_text(s)\nfor mode in ('centroid','union'):\n t=s.replace(\\\"'identity_content': 'exact'\\\", \\\"'identity_content': '\\\"+mode+\\\"'\\\",1)\n t=t.replace(\\\"identity_content='exact'\\\", \\\"identity_content='\\\"+mode+\\\"'\\\",1)\n Path('/workspace/task_'+mode+'.py').write_text(t)\nprint('Prepared candidate.py, task_centroid.py, task_union.py')\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
